 "_note": "Blacktown International Sportspark, Oval 1 (Rooty Hill, Sydney). Stage 1 (2026-11-22): the boundary fence is one smooth curve (fence_fourier) fitted to the NSW 7.5 cm aerial; the grandstand's roof footprint and 11 m height come from Google Earth's 3D mesh (straight-down shots, roof front 0.3 m over the fence, 24.5 m deep). Seat rows (11, 1.0-5.4 m) are estimated from the published 1,600 seats, not measured. Stage 2 (2026-11-22): heights read off Google Earth's status bar on a 3 m grid and on radial lines round the bank (whole metres); detail.py models the open gallery and columns on the stand's back, the roof masts (16 m tops), the floodlights under the roof, the 8 m south wing and its raised walkway, the indoor centre (roof 6-7 m, monitors 8 m) and two stairs up the bank; the north roof end is cut on its real line (end_skew); light towers stand at Google Earth's head positions (44.5 m); the bank and the dirt path on its top follow the measured terrain table. Not yet built: the surroundings beyond the bank (stage 3); the ground beyond 35 m out from the fence is held at the last measured height.",
